[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'I have fixed the code in `retry.py` to handle the `Retry-After` header case-insensitively.\n\nThe original implementation only looked for the lowercase key `"retry-after"`, which caused it to return `None` when the header was provided in a different casing (e.g., `"Retry-After"`), as seen in the failing test.\n\nI updated `parse_retry_after` to iterate through the headers and perform a case-insensitive comparison on the keys.\n\n```python\ndef parse_retry_after(headers):\n    """Seconds to wait before retrying, or None if the header is absent."""\n    for k, v in headers.items():\n        if k.lower() == "retry-after":\n            return int(v)\n    return None\n```\n\nI verified the fix by running `python -m pytest tests`, and the test now passes.', 'extras': {'signature': 'Ej0KOwERTTIPzSRJjEPUos4chfMSv+SfhrFJRMZ/WoB3gFFVkuzzw6TCML4xLQn2qaXY6dWUDgScFGydz6oM'}}]
